Subject: [LANDED round 237 under Decisions 95/96] close the bottom W level in horizontal Redi masks

Status: LANDED in round 237 as one member of the source-exact pair authorised
by Decisions 95/96.  The historical round-229 measurement below is retained
unchanged.  The production-JIT R16 replay makes hmsku/hmskv and
A13/A23 bit-exact, but reduces the maximum tracer-LDF RHS error only from
7.2621621143171395e-11 to 4.8307864472774789e-11 K/s (33.48%).  This
refutes the preregistered >=90% closure threshold.  The remaining horizontal
face-thickness and vertical-flux seams must be resolved before this source-
exact statement is reconsidered; production was restored after measurement.

Compiled source: VORTEX_SMT3_VEC_R16_OMIP_L1_P3/BLD/ppsrc/nemo/
traldf_iso.f90:246-249.  The deepest tracer level reads wmask(jpk)=0;
JAX's periodic roll instead reads the surface W level unless closed explicitly.

diff --git a/packages/ocean/legoesm/ocean/physics/lateral_mixing/gm_redi_latlon_cgrid.py b/packages/ocean/legoesm/ocean/physics/lateral_mixing/gm_redi_latlon_cgrid.py
